5. Storage Replication

Copying data from one storage system to another.

Purpose
Disaster Recovery
Backup
Geo-redundancy
Synchronous Replication

Write acknowledged only after both sites write successfully.

App → Site A
       ↓
     Site B


RPO = 0

Higher latency.

Asynchronous Replication

Write first locally.

Replicate later.

Every minute
Every five minutes


Lower latency.

Small data-loss window.

Interview Question

Difference between RPO and RTO?

RPO = acceptable data loss
RTO = acceptable downtime
NetApp

NetApp SnapMirror is a major replication technology.

