13. Distributed Storage Architecture

This is the highest-value topic.

Problem

Single storage appliance becomes bottleneck.

Need petabytes of data.

Need billions of files.

Need no single point of failure.

Distributed Storage

Many nodes act as one storage system.

Client
   |
Cluster
 ├ Node1
 ├ Node2
 ├ Node3
 └ Node4

Benefits
Scale Out

Add nodes.

Capacity increases.

Performance increases.

Fault Tolerance

If one node fails:

Node1 ❌
Node2 ✅
Node3 ✅


System keeps running.

Data Distribution

Data spread across nodes.

Replication ensures durability.

Concepts Often Asked
Consistent Hashing

Determines where data lives.

Replication Factor
3 copies


stored on separate nodes.

Quorum

Majority agreement before commit.

Rebalancing

Redistributes data when nodes are added/removed.

